// KNOWN-GAP.
//
// Same violation as the control, bad_dyn_escape_direct.exsc: Right's
// real mark (alloc, rete) exceeds the {alloc} bound the returned dyn
// value claims. The only difference is that the cast's operand here has
// an ABSTRACT type T, bound to Summable by `box`'s own generic
// parameter, rather than the concrete type Right. Sec 4.4's EXS-E0510
// check is stated at the CAST SITE, against a concrete implementation --
// but a cast inside a generic function never has one: `box` is compiled
// once (Sec 7.1), before any T is chosen, so there is no impl for
// check_dyn_casts_in_func() to compare against, by construction. The
// checker accepts this file.
//
// Composed with a caller that instantiates `box<Right>`, this is a real
// capability escape: `box<Right>(r)` hands back a value stamped
// `dyn Summable poscit {alloc}`, and a caller who trusts that stamp (the
// entire point of a dyn bound, per Sec 4.4) and grants only `alloc` will
// nonetheless invoke a `combine` that needs `rete`. Nothing catches this
// anywhere in the pipeline modeled here -- not at `box`'s own definition
// (it declares and uses nothing itself), not at the cast (T is
// abstract), and not at Right's own definition (its mark is internally
// consistent, see bad_static_impl_exceeds_member_ceiling.exsc for that
// separate, only-checkable-with-the-experimental-flag question).
//
// The shape a fix would need is NOT a smarter cast-site check -- the
// cast site fundamentally cannot see past an abstract T. It is the same
// fix bad_static_impl_exceeds_member_ceiling.exsc's --strict-static-
// ceiling experiment models: enforce, at EVERY `interfacies ... in ...
// poscit ...` declaration, that the impl's mark cannot exceed the
// trait's own declared per-member ceiling. If that held, Right's
// declaration -- not `box`, not the cast, not the call site -- would be
// the thing that fails to compile, and the dyn bound `box` manufactures
// would be trustworthy by construction, because every impl of Summable,
// known or future, would already be inside it.

interfacies Summable {
    functio combine(self, other: f32) -> f32 poscit alloc
}

functio usa_rete(x: f32) -> f32 poscit rete {
    redde x;
}

interfacies Summable in Right poscit alloc, rete {
    functio combine(self, other: f32) -> f32 {
        redde usa_rete(other);
    }
}

publica functio box<T: Summable>(x: T) -> dyn Summable poscit {alloc} {
    redde x sicut dyn Summable poscit {alloc};
}
